<section id="adaptable">
  <section>
    <h1>Responsive web design</h1>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>For whom?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Mobile users</li>
      <li>
        People with low vision, who end up on the mobile display of a website
        when using text magnification
      </li>
      <li>Screenreader users with a non-maximized screen.</li>
      <li>People with dyslexia</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Orientation</h2>
    <p>
      The user must be able to choose the orientation of smartphone or tablet:
      portrait or landscape
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Not OK</h2>
    <p>
      <img
        class="stretch"
        src="https://images.anysurfer.be/orientation/retournez_votre_appareil.png"
        alt="urbanlinker.com - Retournez votre appareil"
      />
    </p>

    <aside class="notes">
      Il vaut mieux proposer un design moins optimal que de complètement bloquer
      l'access au contenu.
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Resize text</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a
          target="tweede"
          target="tweede"
          href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG20/quickref/#qr-visual-audio-contrast-scale">
          Magnification up to 200%
        </a>{' '}
        without losing content (e.g. overlap)
      </li>
      <li>Browser zoom (cmd of ctrl +)</li>
      <li>Is all content still visible on the mobile display?</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Reflow</h2>
    <p>When content is viewed in a viewport of 320 CSS pixels:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>No loss of content or functionality</li>
      <li>No horizontal scrolling</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To test: 1280 wide viewport with 400% zoom</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Manage your sticky headers/footers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>They can make a page unusable with zoom</li>
      <li>
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Techniques/css/C34">
          Use Media queries to 'unstick' a header/footer
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2></h2>
    <h2>Text spacing</h2>
    <p>No loss of content or functionality when adjusting style properties:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Line height (line spacing): at least 1.5 times font size;</li>
      <li>Space following paragraphs: at least 2 times font size;</li>
      <li>Letter spacing (tracking): at least 0.12 times font size;</li>
      <li>Word spacing: at least 0.16 times font size.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a
        target="tweede"
        target="tweede"
        href="https://developer.paciellogroup.com/blog/2018/05/short-note-on-getting-spaced-out-with-sc-1-4-12-text-spacing/">
        Testscript via bookmark
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Example: Sporza</h2>
    <img
      class="stretch"
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/text_spacing/sporza_normal.png"
      alt="text under a photo with standard spacing"
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Example: Sporza with more spaces (not OK)</h2>
    <img
      class="stretch"
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/text_spacing/sporza_text_spacing.png"
      alt="Texte plus espacé, partiellement troncqué"
    />
    <aside class="notes">
      Les contenants doivent s'adapter à la taille du contenu.
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Don't disable pinch to zoom</h2>
    <pre class=""><code is:raw>&lt;meta content="width=device-width;initial-scale=1.0;
maximum-scale=1.0; user-scalable=1;" name="viewport" /&gt;</code></pre>

    <pre class=""><code is:raw>&lt;meta name="viewport" content="user-scalable=no" /&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>
</section>
